    "https://careers.ua.edu/jobs/search/education": {
      "title": "College of Education",
      "description": "College of Education My settings Life at UA Campus Life Tuscaloosa Benefits Work Life Search Jobs Job Alerts Veterans Faculty Jobs Staff Jobs Student Jobs UA System Jobs My Application Kiosk mode College of Education For over 150 years, the College of Education has been dedicated to developing professionals with the expertise needed to advance the intellectual and social conditions of all learners. By effectively preparing graduates to pursue their pedagogical and scholarly endeavors, the College of Education aims to lead Alabama in teaching, scholarship, advocacy, and service. Our faculty’s research, teaching, and service is widely recognized through their securement of external funding, national awards, professional organization leadership, established centers and offices, and outreach to the local, state, and national communities. Faculty in the college are free to pursue their passions, partner with the local communities, and excel in their many pursuits of academia. The College of Education consists of six academic departments and 29 high-caliber programs, including opportunities that enable students to earn specialized degrees in teacher education, exercise science, and educational neuroscience. Through a robust offering of main campus options, online degrees, and certification programs, the College is poised to accommodate any learner. The College of Education is also home to the No. 1 competitive adaptive sports program in the nation, UA Adapted Athletics, and proudly supports their successes at their state-of-the-art facilities. With teaching, research, and outreach efforts that serve the local community and beyond, the College of Education continues to expand its footprint in both the world of academia and in our global society. The College of Education is committed to advancing opportunities for all of its community members, including increasing and retaining faculty, staff, and students from a range of backgrounds and areas of expertise, creating a culture that welcomes a vibrant and global college community, and providing opportunities for faculty, staff, and students to develop competencies that support these efforts. For more information on the College of Education’s commitments and efforts, please visit our website: https://education.ua.edu/ Skip to jobs search results Category Search categories 3 filter options found Category Non-Tenure-Track/Clinical Faculty (3 items) 3 Temporary Part Time Faculty (1 items) 1 Tenure/Tenure-Track Faculty (4 items) 4 Employment Type Search employment types 2 filter options found Employment Type Regular Full-time (Benefits eligible) (7 items) 7 Temporary Part-time (No benefits) (1 items) 1 Department/Organization Search 4 filter options found Department/Organization 212401 - Curriculum and Instruction (5 items) 5 212501 - Ed Leadership/Policy/Tech Studies (1 items) 1 212701 - Special Education (1 items) 1 212801 - Kinesiology (1 items) 1 Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Edu - Assistant Professor of Exercise Science – Renewable Contract - 530503 Non-Tenure-Track/Clinical Faculty Regular Full-time (Benefits eligible) 212801 - Kinesiology The Department of Kinesiology at The University of Alabama invites applications for a full-time, renewable contract (non-tenure track) faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor in Exercise Science, beginning August 2027. Read more Edu - Assistant Professor of Elementary Mathematics Education - Tenure/Tenure Track - 530441 Tenure/Tenure-Track Faculty Regular Full-time (Benefits eligible) 212401 - Curriculum and Instruction The Department of Curriculum and Instruction in the College of Education at The University of Alabama is seeking a full-time, tenure-track assistant professor of elementary education (grades PreK-6) with expertise in mathematics education. Read more Edu - Assistant Professor/Associate Professor of Instructional Technology- Tenure/Tenure Track-530461 Tenure/Tenure-Track Faculty Regular Full-time (Benefits eligible) 212501 - Ed Leadership/Policy/Tech Studies The Department of Educational Leadership, Policy and Technology Studies at The University of Alabama invites applications for an Assistant or Associate Professor of Instructional Technology, preferably a scholar whose research and teaching focus on the educational applications of artificial intelligence in teaching, learning, instructional design, and educational research.\nThe Department of Educational Leadership, Policy, and Technology Studies at the University of Alabama invites applications for an Assistant or Associate Professor of Instructional Technology position. Read more Edu - Assistant Professor of Special Education - Tenure/Tenure Track - 530371 Tenure/Tenure-Track Faculty Regular Full-time (Benefits eligible) 212701 - Special Education Appointments to the faculty of The University of Alabama are based on the personnel requirements of the University’s academic programs and on the goal of achieving and maintaining excellence in its teaching, research, and service/academic citizenship activities.\n\nThe Department of Special Education in the College of Education at The University of Alabama invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Special Education. We seek a collaborative scholar and educator whose research, teaching, and service contribute to the preparation of highly effective special education professionals and to improved outcomes for children, youth, and adults with disabilities.\n\nThe successful candidate will join a nationally recognized special education faculty with opportunities to contribute across undergraduate and graduate programs, including collaborative special education, early childhood special education, autism, and related areas. The department offers baccalaureate, Master's, education specialist, Ed.D., and Ph.D. programs, including online graduate programs in the Masters, Ed,S. and Ed.D programs.\n\nThe University of Alabama's Department of Special Education prepares educators and professionals to support learners with and at risk for disabilities across the lifespan. Current programs include undergraduate preparation in special education and the Multiple Abilities Program, as well as graduate programs spanning collaborative special education, early childhood special education, learning disabilities, gifted education, autism, severe disabilities, and related areas Read more Edu - Clinical Assistant Professor of Elementary Literacy Education – Renewable Contract-53033 Non-Tenure-Track/Clinical Faculty Regular Full-time (Benefits eligible) 212401 - Curriculum and Instruction Appointments to the faculty of The University of Alabama are based on the personnel requirements of the University’s academic programs and on the goal of achieving and maintaining excellence in its teaching, research, and service/academic citizenship activities.\n\nThe Department of Curriculum and Instruction in the College of Education at The University of Alabama invites applications for a full-time, Clinical Assistant Professor of Elementary Education (grades PreK–6) with a specific interest in Literacy Education Read more Edu- Assistant/Associate Professor of Elementary Literacy Education-Tenure/Tenure Track - 530315 Tenure/Tenure-Track Faculty Regular Full-time (Benefits eligible) 212401 - Curriculum and Instruction The Department of Curriculum and Instruction in the College of Education at The University of Alabama invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant/Associate Professor of Elementary Education (grades PreK–6) with a specific interest in Literacy Education. Read more Edu - Clinical Assistant Professor of Elementary Education Mathematics– Renewable Contract - 530088 Non-Tenure-Track/Clinical Faculty Regular Full-time (Benefits eligible) 212401 - Curriculum and Instruction The Department of Curriculum and Instruction in the College of Education at The University of Alabama is seeking a full-time, clinical assistant professor of elementary education (grades PreK-6) with expertise in mathematics education. The University of Alabama is a Research I institution with considerable emphasis on recruiting productive scholars and effective instructors. This is a nine-month, non-tenure earning position with a contract of three years, eligible for renewal. Read more Edu - College of Education - Temporary Clinical Supervisor (Internship, Practicum, and Field Experiences) - 528914 Temporary Part Time Faculty Temporary Part-time (No benefits) 212401 - Curriculum and Instruction The College of Education seeks qualified candidates for a rolling pool of Clinical Supervisors to support teacher candidates during internship, practicum, and field experiences. Read more Displaying all 8 entries Interested in Joining the College of Education? Please fill out the information below to join the COE talent network First Name (required) 35dbe133 Last Name (required) 9779c907 Email (required) f6cef7af Employment Type 92aae04c Tenure Track Non-Tenure Track Clinical Faculty Administration Part-Time Temporary Academic Departments 79cce3ba Curriculum & Instruction Educational Leadership, Policy, & Tech. Studies Educational Studies Kinesiology Music Education Special Education & Multiple Abilities Upload CV 09fd3961 Accepted formats: PDF, DOC, DOCX, RTF, ODT, XML, DOT, PNG, GIF, JPG, JPEG, ZIP Join UA Talent Network Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you for your interest in joining The University of Alabama FOLLOW US Accessibility | Equal Opportunity | About This Site | Webmaster Copyright © 2021 The University of Alabama | Disclaimer | Privacy | Accessibility × Before You Go... Would You Like To Register For Job Alerts? First Name (required) 17a5242b Last Name (required) abb09f4c Email (required) 869d3d4b Select from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs. b739fdea Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Employment Type Submit Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you! Close Candidate Details × This website uses cookies to collect information to improve your browsing experience. Please review our Privacy Statement for more information. I do not accept I accept Please choose the employment type(s)"
